var e={"players/accounts":`Every player account the node knows: identities, wallets, inventory, sessions, bans and notes in one place. Search by username, e-mail, device or custom id; open an account to act on it.`,"players/group_challenges":`Cooperative goals shared by a group (guild, party, friends list): progress is pooled and rewards go to every contributor. Created by the game through the server API or here as templates.`,"players/bans":`Active and expired bans, with the rule that fired and who issued it. Unban here or from the account page; appeals land under Settings → Sanctions.`,"players/ban_rules":`Reason codes and automatic rules (N chat reports, anti-cheat verdicts, fraud flags) that turn into bans or mutes. Rules run on the node; the first match wins.`,"players/chat_reports":`Chat messages reported by players, with context lines around them. Resolve, warn, mute or ban from here; the filter stats live under Social → Chat filters.`,"players/access":`Who may log in at all: open, allowlist-only or closed, per provider and per environment (staging, soak, launch day). Denied attempts show up under Access denials.`,"players/allowlist":`Accounts, e-mails and device ids allowed through a closed Access policy — the playtest / friends-and-family list. Entries can carry a note and an expiry.`,"players/denials":`Login attempts the Access policy refused: when, which provider and why (not on the list, closed, country blocked). Rows appear as players hit a closed door.`,"players/auth_providers":`Identity providers players can sign in with: device, e-mail, Steam, Apple, Google, custom JWT… Toggle, order and configure them; linking rules live on the account.`,"players/device_codes":`Pending device-code logins (TV / console / headless clients): the short code a player types on the web to pair a device. Revoke a code before it is claimed.`,"players/login_queue":`Launch-day waiting room: when the node is above its login budget, players queue here with a position and ETA. Flush it to let everyone in at once.`,"players/data_rights":`GDPR / CCPA requests — export, erase, restrict — with their state and deadline. Exports are produced by the node; erasure anonymises the account and its ledger.`,"players/reports":`Chat reports, UGC reports and player complaints in one moderation queue: resolve, warn, mute or ban from the row.`,"players/moderation":`Moderation queue: reports from chat, UGC and players, with the action taken and who took it.`,"players/providers":`Identity providers players can sign in with and how accounts link across them.`,"content/versions":`Content versions published to clients: what each contains, where it is hosted and who receives it.`,"world/worlds":`Persistent seamless worlds: cells, which server owns which cell, entities and handovers. Open a world for its map and live state.`,"players/crashes":`Crash reports uploaded by game clients and servers, grouped by signature with versions, platforms and affected users. Mark resolved once a fix ships.`,"servers/fleets":`A fleet keeps N dedicated servers warm in a region and scales between min and max on demand. Open a fleet for its servers, metrics, cost, alerts and scaling policy.`,"servers/servers":`Every dedicated game server the orchestrator runs or knows about: fleet, region, build, allocation and health. Open one for logs, counters and actions.`,"servers/capacity":`Host pool capacity: machines registered through [fleet.ssh] or a [fleet.capacity] provider, how many slots they offer and what is used. Reconcile re-reads the pools.`,"servers/builds":"Server builds and client artifacts uploaded with `musubi build push`: versions, sizes, chunks and which fleets run them. Roll a fleet to a build from the fleet page.","servers/session_placements":`Placement requests waiting for a server: who asked, the constraints (region, build, capacity) and how long they have waited. Stuck rows usually mean no fleet matches.`,"servers/placements":`Placement strategies: how a session is matched to a region and fleet (latency, cost, fill-first, spread). Offers show what each strategy would pick right now.`,"servers/edge":`The UDP edge proxy terminates game traffic on the node, hides server addresses and blocks abusive sources. Status, counters and the block list live here when it runs.`,"servers/storage_endpoints":`S3-compatible buckets the node uses for builds, replays, exports and UGC. Endpoint, bucket, credentials reference and which role writes there.`,"servers/hosts":`Machines in the host pool (bare metal / VMs reached over SSH) that run dedicated servers. Probe, drain and undrain; a notice schedules maintenance.`,"servers/host_classes":`Hardware classes for the host pool (CPU, memory, cost per hour) used by placement and the cost view. Defined in config or by the capacity provider.`,"servers/aliases":"Named allocation targets the game uses instead of fleet ids — `prod-eu`, `playtest` — so a fleet swap or a region move is a one-row change here.","servers/client_versions":`Minimum and recommended client version per platform, with store links and a maintenance flag. Out-of-date clients are told to update at login.`,"servers/countries":`ISO country table with blocked flag and age restriction per country. Blocking refuses logins from that country; groups drive routing and pricing.`,"servers/country_groups":`Named sets of countries (EU, LATAM, China-excluded…) for routing, pricing and content rules. A country can be in several groups.`,"liveops/timeline":`Everything scheduled against the calendar — live events, offers, news, experiments, config changes — on one time axis. Overlaps and gaps are visible at a glance.`,"liveops/live_events":`Time-boxed events with their own rewards, leaderboards and content toggles. Draft → scheduled → live → ended; the game reads the active set at login and on change.`,"liveops/flags":`Feature flags with audience targeting and percentage rollout; evaluated on the node and pushed to clients live. Open a flag for its history and kill switch.`,"liveops/experiments":`A/B tests: variants, allocation, audience and the metrics they are judged on. Results are computed from the node's own analytics store.`,"liveops/configs":`Remote config documents (JSON) versioned and targeted by audience, with instant rollout and rollback. Clients receive the merged view.`,"liveops/audiences":`Reusable player segments — new, paying, platform, country, custom attributes — used by flags, configs, offers, news and push.`,"liveops/news":`In-game news and message-of-the-day posts, localised and targeted, with publish windows. Read receipts feed the analytics store.`,"liveops/offers":`Personalised store offers: who sees what, at which price, for how long, with purchase limits. Offers reference store items and audiences.`,"liveops/changesets":`Bundled economy / content changes reviewed and applied atomically — the LiveOps release unit. Diff, approve, apply, roll back.`,"liveops/zanshin":`The Zanshin LiveOps integration: external campaigns and segments synchronised into the node. Status of the link and last sync.`,"liveops/webhooks":`Outgoing webhooks: which events are delivered to which URL, with signing secret, retries and delivery log. Failing endpoints are flagged on the overview.`,"liveops/sweepstakes":`Raffles and giveaways with entry rules, draw time and prize table. Draws run on the node and are recorded for audit.`,"liveops/tutorials":`Tutorial and onboarding step definitions with completion tracking per player — used to gate rewards and to measure drop-off in the funnel.`,"liveops/push":`Push-notification campaigns (APNs / FCM) with audience, schedule and template; delivery stats come back per campaign.`,"liveops/workflows":`Automations: when X happens, do Y — grant on milestone, mute on report threshold, notify on fleet alert. Each run is logged.`,"economy/currencies":`Soft and hard currencies, their caps, decimals and whether they are tradable. Every balance change goes through the ledger.`,"economy/items":`The item catalog: types, rarity, stack sizes, tags and attributes the game reads. Open an item for its full definition and where it is referenced.`,"economy/reward_tables":`Weighted loot tables with nested rolls, pity and guarantees. Reward modifiers and VIP tiers can scale them.`,"economy/reward_modifiers":`Multipliers applied on top of reward tables and grants — double-XP weekends, VIP bonuses, event boosts — with audience and time window.`,"economy/store":`Store items: what is sold for which currency or real-money product, with limits and availability windows. Offers personalise these.`,"economy/coupons":`Promo coupons: code pattern, redemption limits, grant and expiry. Redemptions are counted per account.`,"economy/entitlements":`Entitlements granted by purchases, subscriptions or operators: battle pass, DLC, premium — what unlocks and until when.`,"economy/progression":`Progression tracks (player level, battle pass, mastery) with tiers and rewards. Open a track to edit tiers.`,"economy/quests":`Daily / weekly / story quests: objectives bound to game events, rewards, reroll rules. Emit a test event to see progress move.`,"economy/quest_pools":`Pools hand out N quests per rotation from a set; accelerate or retire a pool without touching the quests themselves.`,"economy/seasons":`Seasons group tracks, leaderboards and resets into a calendar period. Open a season for its timeline and reset rules.`,"economy/hero_classes":`Character / hero / class definitions with base stats and unlock rules — reference data the game reads at login.`,"economy/crafting":`Crafting recipes: inputs, outputs, time and cost. Crafting is validated and executed on the node.`,"economy/ads":`Rewarded-ad placements and their rewards, with caps per player per day and SSV verification status.`,"economy/achievements":`Achievements with hidden / incremental variants and platform mapping (Steam, PSN, Game Center).`,"economy/graphs":`Dependency graph of the economy — what grants what, what unlocks what — generated from the catalog to spot loops and dead ends.`,"economy/root":`The economy root document: global rules, default currency, rounding and ledger retention.`,"economy/streaks":`Login and activity streaks with escalating rewards and grace days.`,"economy/energy":`Energy / stamina systems: cap, regen rate, refill price and per-action costs.`,"economy/challenge_templates":`Templates for group and personal challenges: objective, duration, reward; instantiated by the game or a workflow.`,"economy/iap_products":`Real-money products as the stores know them (SKU per platform) mapped to what they grant. Receipts are validated on the node.`,"economy/subscription_plans":`Recurring subscriptions per platform with grace periods and the entitlements they keep active.`,"economy/vip":`VIP tiers earned by spend or activity, with their perks and reward modifiers.`,"economy/donations":`Player-to-player and player-to-creator donations: rules, fees and limits.`,"economy/codes":`Single-use and campaign codes (keys, gift codes) generated in batches; redemptions and remaining counts per batch.`,"economy/key_groups":`Groups of generated keys for distribution (press, giveaways, retail) with activation tracking.`,"economy/inventory_ops":`Bulk inventory operations — grant, revoke, migrate item ids — against an audience, previewed before they run.`,"economy/grant_limits":`Caps on what operators and workflows may grant per day, to contain mistakes and compromised keys.`,"economy/inventory_limits":`Per-player inventory caps by item type and slot; the node refuses grants above them.`,"economy/strings":`Localised economy strings (item names, descriptions) per locale, exported to the client.`,"economy/fraud":`Fraud signals: refunds, chargebacks, impossible balances, receipt replay. Review and sanction from here.`,"content/bundles":`Content versions and bundles published to clients: what each version contains, where it is hosted and who receives it (channel, audience).`,"content/content_tags":`Tags used to target content and configs (platform, locale, tier). Reference data for bundles and schedules.`,"content/config_sources":`Where remote config comes from — Git repository, S3 bucket, this console — and how often it is pulled. The node validates before applying.`,"content/storage_schemas":`JSON schemas for player storage collections: the node validates writes against them and migrates on version bump.`,"content/modules":`Server-side modules (Rust / WASM) loaded by the node: version, hooks they implement, resource usage. Open a module to reload or inspect.`,"content/schedules":`Scheduled content switches: which bundle or config becomes active when, per channel. Rows appear as you schedule a change.`,"content/ugc":`User-generated content: uploads, moderation queue, reports and takedowns. Items wait here until approved when moderation is on.`,"social/chat_filters":`Profanity and pattern filters applied to chat on the node, per locale, with actions (mask, block, report). Test a phrase against the live rules.`,"social/stats":`Player statistics definitions and global aggregates; per-player values and history are on the account page.`,"social/rating":`Skill rating configuration (TrueSkill / Glicko / Elo) per mode and the current distribution.`,"social/matchmaker":`Queues, rules and pools of the matchmaker; live wait times and open matches. Pause or drain a queue before a deploy.`,"social/mm_stats":`Matchmaking outcomes over time: time-to-match, match quality, cancellations, by queue and region.`,"social/mm_rejections":`Tickets the matchmaker refused and why (no pool, constraints too tight, banned). Rows appear as players queue.`,"social/matches":`Authoritative and relayed matches running right now, with module, tick and host node.`,"social/turns":`Asynchronous turn-based matches: whose turn, deadlines and timeouts.`,"social/sessions":`Live realtime sessions (lobbies, parties, rooms) with members and host. Kick or close a session.`,"social/tournaments":`Scheduled and live tournaments with brackets or score ladders: category, window, records and bracket state. Create one to open registration.`,"social/async_mm":`Asynchronous matchmaking: ghost / replay opponents picked by skill when no live player is waiting.`,"social/streams":`Live streams registered by the game (spectator, replay, co-stream): who streams what to how many viewers.`,"social/referrals":`Referral programme: codes, invites, conversions and rewards on both sides.`,"world/cluster_worlds":`Worlds as placed across the cluster: node, cells, load, hibernation. Unplaced worlds are flagged on the overview.`,"world/netsim":`Network simulation on the node — latency, loss, jitter per lane — for chaos tests without touching the OS.`,"cluster/nodes":`Nodes in the cluster with roles, region, heartbeat and version.`,"cluster/matches":`Where every match runs, by node.`,"cluster/mesh_net":`WireGuard-style mesh between nodes: peers, keys and reachability. Enable it in the node config for multi-host clusters.`,"cluster/geoip":`GeoIP database used for region routing and country rules: source, version and last update. Update pulls a fresh file.`,"cluster/chunking":`Content-defined chunk store behind builds: dedup ratio, orphans, last GC.`,"cluster/reports":`Daily analytics reports generated by the node.`,"cluster/logs":`Node logs, live tail per node, filtered by level and target.`,"cluster/loadtests":`Synthetic load tests run from the node itself (login storm, match churn, chat flood) with their results.`,"analytics/overview":`Active users, retention, revenue, crashes and reports computed from the node's own event store.`,"analytics/events":`Event names, counts and schemas as the clients send them.`,"analytics/reports":`Daily reports generated by the node — KPIs, retention cohorts, revenue — kept as documents you can download or forward.`,"analytics/sinks":`Where telemetry is forwarded: ClickHouse, S3, Kafka, HTTP. Buffer state, lag and last flush per sink.`,"analytics/crashes":`Crash reports live under Players → Crash reports.`,"settings/keys":`Server keys with roles and scopes for game servers, tools and CI. Rotate and revoke here; usage is in the audit log.`,"settings/operators":`Operators of this console: role, how they sign in (password, key, SSO) and last login. Add, reset passwords, change roles.`,"settings/invites":`Pending operator invitations with role and expiry. Invite by e-mail; the link sets the password.`,"settings/jwt_keys":`Signing keys for player session tokens, with rotation and overlap windows. Clients verify against the JWKS endpoint.`,"settings/accounts_policy":`Account rules: username constraints, e-mail verification, linking limits, inactivity deletion.`,"settings/audit":`Every write made through the API: who, when, what, with the request body. Filter by actor, route or account.`,"settings/sso":`Single sign-on for operators (OIDC): issuer, client, role mapping.`,"settings/config":`The effective node configuration with sources and overrides. Edit the live-reloadable part here.`,"settings/environments":`Environments (dev, staging, prod) and what differs between them: keys, providers, policies.`,"settings/oauth":`OAuth clients that may call the API on behalf of operators or tools: ids, scopes, redirect URIs.`,"settings/legal":`Terms, privacy policy and age gates per region, with versions players must accept.`,"settings/sanctions":`Bans, mutes and warnings across the project with appeals and history.`,"settings/deletions":`Account deletions pending the grace period, and what will be erased.`,"settings/secrets":`Secrets referenced by config and integrations (provider keys, bucket credentials) — stored encrypted, shown only by name.`,"settings/devtools":`Developer tools: generate test accounts, emit events, reset a player, clear caches. Disabled outside dev environments.`};export{e as t};